Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0166): laptop packages 158-161 (ES02
 0.177-0.197) merged; CSV frozen columns redraw without a frame

- Packages 158 (bc2891cc), 159 (22603f5f), 160 (2afc1946), 161 (b8ea3a51) merged
  in order, three-way on each package's _machine_ai/base_*. Every machine feature
  is still in (likeF5, viaLinks, stopF5Build, freeProgram, skipBuildIfUpToDate,
  applyLayout, pinClaudeTabs, replaceHits, markJump, filelog, ...).
  test/smoke_extension.js conflicted at 158 / 159 and stayed behind, so 160 / 161
  merged onto it without those packages' changes (3 event-wiring failures: the
  generator now writes gen.cpp + gen.h + a part file) -> package 161's whole
  (the machine's 89 test titles and 22 machine test blocks are all in it).
- media/csv.js: the redraw after a sideways scroll waited for the next animation
  frame only; when none came (this PC's headless Edge; a hidden window) it never
  redrew and no later scroll asked again -- the frozen columns scrolled away
  (A 52 -> -248). Now drawn after 40 ms if the frame has not come.
- Not run on the machine: test/e2e_all.js (edits the tree and builds 9050),
  test/vscode_run_it.ps1 (builds and starts wb_serve).

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (lib 192, probe incl. freeze columns, extension 257,
panels); real VS Code 159/159 -- all pass for the first time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
